A||N||6||Will||Our new curb ornament (pics)||||1||
Z||000000||Will||07-31-2001||06:16 PM||||Just finished the mechanicals of a 74 XJ6 Jaguar, with a twist:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Front_Engine.jpg"> <P>The engine is a 400 SBC, with TPI modified to fit, and an HEI/optispark Hybrid distributor run by '95 LT1 electronics.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Intake_Tract.jpg"> <P>Using MAF with dual K&N's in a rather ingenuitive cold air setup.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fan.jpg"> <P>Somewhat rare 240W electric fan (GM).<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Waterpump_Pulley_2.jpg"> <P>Dual belt waterpumpt pulley.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Left_Front_2.jpg"> <P>The mechanicals are all done, but the car still needs its body and interior work. At least it's out of the garage. Now I can work on my Northstar!<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Big_Cat_Little_Cat.jpg"> <P>Big Cat, Little Cat<P>I'll post some full engine compartment view later.||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||07-31-2001||07:16 PM||||Are they Grand National wheels?I noticed the car looks a little dinged.You should leave it that way,what a sleeper.Or to go the other way,It would make a very unique show car.What kind of drive train did you use?When do you expect to get it on the road?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||07-31-2001||10:58 PM||||Actually those are vintage Jaguar steel wheels.<BR>We have a set of later Jaguar alloys which will go on it eventually.<P>Actually, pending state inspection, it <I>is</I> on the road, in that it can move under its own power limited primarily by the quantity of fuel it's carrying.<BR>It's using a 4L60E transmission with the stock Jaguar rear end and suspension.<BR>We put the hood back on it shortly after these pictures were taken.<BR>As you can see, it has some damage to the left front fender, a couple of small dings on the right front fender, and a patch of primer on the left rear quarter panel. We're thinking about painting it Old English White, in honor of the totaled car it's replacing.<BR>The interior is mostly out right now while we chase down rust, replace seatbelts, etc.<BR>The engine, from the old car, is closing in on 300,000 miles and was installed using a modified version of a kit produced by John's Cars in Dallas, TX.<P>Currently, we have no intention of showing it, just making it a daily driver alongside all our other frankensteined cars (the suburban you see in the background of the last picture has a Caddillac 500 V8, we also have a Datsun 280Z with an LT1 style engine, and my Fiero Northstar soon to join the pack).||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||08-01-2001||12:35 AM||||Did that Jag come with fuel injection stock? The reason I ask is that my Dad wants to switch his 68 E-type (4.2 L I-6) to fuel injection. I was wondering what kit you used.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||08-01-2001||09:31 AM||||Looks good! I was gonna do that to my XJS had I kept it...<P>I am surprised that the hood closed. The air filter unit looks a little high. Good job of packing it in there...<P>Let us know how she does when you get her on the street...<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||08-03-2001||02:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B>Did that Jag come with fuel injection stock? The reason I ask is that my Dad wants to switch his 68 E-type (4.2 L I-6) to fuel injection. I was wondering what kit you used.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Stock it had the Jag 4.2 I6.<BR>Now it has 400 SBC with TPI injection.<BR>We used a John's Cars kit. I don't know if they have a website or not.<P>Your friend could find a later XJ6 with the injected 4.2 and transfer the injection hardware from that car to his car. Or just swap the whole engine over, if he doesn't mind the numbers not matching.<P>If he's not a purist, he might try GM's new Vortec 4200. It's a 4.2 litre DOHC I6 that makes 270 HP and 270 ftlbs.<BR>That engine would be awesome in an E-type with a T56 6 speed.<BR>If you're a British Car Purist, please don't lynch me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||08-03-2001||02:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>Looks good! I was gonna do that to my XJS had I kept it...<P>I am surprised that the hood closed. The air filter unit looks a little high. Good job of packing it in there...<P>Let us know how she does when you get her on the street...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The inside of the hood just barely touches the outer ends of the filters. They're pliable...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
